=== Test 7: regression — existing CASE inequality still works ===
== Query ==
SELECT c.c_id, SUM(CASE WHEN c.c_region < 2 THEN o.o_amt ELSE 0 END)
FROM cte_customer AS c
JOIN cte_orders AS o ON o.o_custkey = c.c_id
GROUP BY c.c_id;

Number of output lines, including header: 4

== Diff ==
==========



== Expected result ==
SELECT c.c_id, SUM(CASE WHEN c.c_region < 2 THEN o.o_amt ELSE 0 END)
FROM cte_customer AS c
JOIN cte_orders AS o ON o.o_custkey = c.c_id
GROUP BY c.c_id|
c_id	SUM(CASE WHEN c.c_region < 2 THEN o.o_amt ELSE 0 END)
100	125
200	100
300	0


=== Test 8: rejection — GREATEST with three arguments ===
Expected error: parser rejects 3-arg GREATEST in v1 (n>2 deferred to I.5 v2)
Syntax error in SQL statement: Unexpected at this point
> WITH sums AS (SELECT o_custkey AS k, SUM(o_amt) AS t FROM cte_orders GROUP BY o_custkey) SELECT c.c_id, SUM(GREATEST(sums.k, 100, 200)) FROM cte_customer AS c JOIN sums ON sums.k = c.c_id GROUP BY c.c_id;
!                                                                                                                                 ^
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: Syntax error.


=== Test 9: rejection — GREATEST with two distinct columns ===
Expected error: distinct-column GREATEST deferred to I.5 v2
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: GREATEST/LEAST with two distinct column operands is not yet supported (deferred to I.5 v2 — needs register-based CASE codegen).


=== Test 10: rejection — nullable column operand ===
Expected error: nullable GREATEST/LEAST operands rejected in v1
Error handling: RPE
ronsql_cli caught exception: GREATEST/LEAST on nullable column operands is not yet supported because MySQL NULL propagation would require multi-arm CASE lowering.
